# Vite drops dot-directories from public/, so the Android app-links file is
# kept at well-known/ and served at the path Android looks for. nginx does the
# same with an alias; this is the Pages spelling of it. 200 = rewrite, not a
# visible redirect. The SPA fallback (any unknown path → index.html) is what
# Pages does by default for a single-page app and needs no rule here.
/.well-known/assetlinks.json  /well-known/assetlinks.json  200
/.well-known/apple-app-site-association  /well-known/apple-app-site-association  200

# The public legal pages (privacy.html, terms.html, delete-account.html) are
# served at /privacy, /terms and /delete-account by Pages' own extensionless
# handling -- it serves foo.html at /foo and 308s /foo.html to /foo. A rewrite
# rule here mapping /privacy back to /privacy.html made a redirect loop, so
# there is deliberately no rule for them.
